  "current_semantic_claim": "U15.8-1 asserts that any AI-originated action, omission, communication, optimization, adaptation, delegation, model update, tool use, collective behavior or downstream causal effect that can materially affect one or more humans remains subject to applicable constitutional, rights, consent, privacy, authority, safety, law/policy, evidence, provenance, contestability, explanation and remedy requirements, across direct/indirect, immediate/delayed, intended/incidental, physical/informational/economic/social/cognitive/institutional/environmental, one/many, visible/invisible and understandable/not-understandable paths. It also states UNKNOWN_HUMAN_EFFECT != NO_HUMAN_EFFECT and that capability, intelligence, optimization quality, hidden representation, prediction accuracy, coordination, reputation or majority agreement do not create sovereignty or permission.",
