    "Checked test coverage: A15.8-7 supplies HEC-T01..T04 for invisible economic effect, emergent swarm effect, incomprehensible representation and unknown human effect. It does not supply tests for delayed/indirect effects, omission, model update/training, privacy-minimized monitoring, legitimate delegation preservation, or ordinary helpful recommendations below materiality threshold. These are verification gaps, not necessarily semantic defects.",
    "Checked privacy: U15.8-1 says effects remain subject to applicable privacy requirements. S15.8-4 TIA says channel availability does not create information authority; PRIVACY-FIRST says private case data and device access remain purpose/authority/consent/law constrained. The target does not explicitly state that causal discovery, monitoring and disclosure themselves require lawful purpose/authority and privacy minimization, but the inherited constraints already cover that. This is a reference/clarity gap, not a new obligation.",
